# LINE ENDINGS ARE NOT COSMETIC HERE.
#
# Proved in hytek-lws on 07/09/2026, both directions: a `.mjs` module with CRLF
# makes vitest FAIL TO LOAD IT — "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" —
# while `node --check` and esbuild parse the identical bytes without complaint.
# Worse, vitest blames the file that IMPORTED it, so the error points at a
# comment line in some unrelated test and the real cause is invisible.
#
# CI runs on Linux, checks out LF, and is green. So the failure appears only on
# a developer's Windows machine, after a fresh checkout, on code nobody touched.
# That is the worst shape a bug can have: it teaches people that a red local
# suite means nothing.
#
# .cmd and .ps1 stay CRLF on purpose — PowerShell and cmd want it.
*               text=auto eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.cjs           text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.png           binary
*.webm          binary
